Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Schrödinger Bridges connect two probability distributions with a diffusion process,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.87,0:00:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but nearly every existing solver is heavy: it stacks several neural networks,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.85,0:00:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}needs adversarial min-max training, and can take hours on a GPU.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.99,0:00:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper introduces LightSB, a lightweight Schrödinger Bridge solver.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.58,0:00:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By parameterizing the Schrödinger potential as a Gaussian mixture and treating its logarithm as an energy function,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.01,0:00:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB turns the problem into one simple,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.73,0:00:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}non-minimax optimization objective with closed-form components.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.81,0:00:38.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The result solves Schrödinger Bridges in moderate dimensions in minutes on a CPU,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.04,0:00:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with no painful hyperparameter tuning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.50,0:00:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and is provably a universal approximator of Schrödinger Bridges.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.94,0:00:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The Schrödinger Bridge problem asks for the diffusion process between two given distributions
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.96,0:00:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that stays as close as possible to a reference Wiener process.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.97,0:00:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It is the dynamic version of entropic optimal transport,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.59,0:01:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it underpins applications from single-cell biology to image translation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.51,0:01:08.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The trouble is that almost all existing solvers are heavy-weighted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.85,0:01:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They parameterize the solution with several large neural networks and require complex,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.41,0:01:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}often adversarial optimization.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.42,0:01:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As a result, the field lacks a simple, principled baseline,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.24,0:01:26.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the kind of go-to method that k-means is for clustering or Sinkhorn is for discrete optimal transport.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.14,0:01:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Consider a researcher who simply wants to compute an entropic optimal transport or Schrödinger
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.48,0:01:36.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Bridge between two moderate-dimensional datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.79,0:01:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Today, that means adopting a solver with iterative proportional fitting steps,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.05,0:01:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or min-max optimization,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.67,0:01:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or simulation of the full stochastic process at every training step.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.26,0:01:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}These solvers demand careful neural network design, run for hours on GPUs,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.26,0:01:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and are sensitive to many hyperparameters.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.09,0:02:01.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Yet in many real settings, the user only cares about where the trajectories end,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.49,0:02:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that is, the conditional plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.52,0:02:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This mismatch, heavy machinery for a modest goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.82,0:02:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is exactly the gap LightSB is built to close.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.16,0:02:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes three contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.89,0:02:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, it introduces LightSB,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.62,0:02:21.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a lightweight solver that combines two recent ideas: parameterizing the Schrödinger potential with sum-exp quadratic,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.35,0:02:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that is Gaussian mixture, functions,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.09,0:02:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and viewing the log-potential as an energy function.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.82,0:02:32.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Together these yield a single, non-minimax,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.55,0:02:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}simulation-free optimization objective with closed-form expressions for the plan and the drift.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.28,0:02:39.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.01,0:02:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors prove that this Gaussian-mixture solver is a universal approximator of Schrödinger Bridges,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.74,0:02:47.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which they note is the first ever such result.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.48,0:02:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.21,0:02:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they analyze the generalization error and show it converges at the standard parametric rate as sample size grows.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.24,0:02:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB starts from the goal of minimizing the Kullback-Leibler divergence between the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.51,0:03:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}true entropic optimal transport plan and a parameterized plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.77,0:03:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The obstacle is that we do not know the true plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.04,0:03:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The key move is to exploit the known form of that plan and parameterize only the adjusted Schrödinger potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.31,0:03:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors choose an unnormalized Gaussian mixture for this potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.58,0:03:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Under this choice,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.84,0:03:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}two things become tractable in closed form: the conditional distributions of the plan,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.11,0:03:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the normalization constant.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.38,0:03:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Proposition 3.1 rewrites the KL objective as a simple difference of two expectations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.65,0:03:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}of the log normalization under the source and the log potential under the target,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.91,0:03:42.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which can be estimated by Monte Carlo and optimized with ordinary stochastic gradient descent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.18,0:03:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}No min-max, no iterative proportional fitting,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.45,0:03:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and no simulation of trajectories during training.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.72,0:03:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Once trained, the same potential gives a closed-form drift,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.98,0:03:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the full bridge process can be reconstructed directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.55,0:04:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The solver is tested across four kinds of data.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.76,0:04:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, a two-dimensional Gaussian to Swiss-roll toy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.97,0:04:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which visualizes how the noise level epsilon shapes the trajectories.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.18,0:04:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.39,0:04:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a recent high-dimensional entropic optimal transport benchmark with known ground-truth plans,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.60,0:04:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}spanning dimensions from two to one hundred twenty-eight and several values of epsilon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.80,0:04:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, the MSCI single-cell dataset from a Kaggle competition,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.01,0:04:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with cells from four human donors at four time points, projected by PCA to fifty,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.22,0:04:37.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}one hundred, and one thousand dimensions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.43,0:04:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And fourth, unpaired image translation on FFHQ faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.64,0:04:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}performed in the five-hundred-twelve-dimensional latent space of a pretrained ALAE autoencoder.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.15,0:04:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The results show both accuracy and speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.93,0:04:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the entropic optimal transport benchmark, where the ground truth is known,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.14,0:04:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB reduces the conditional Bures-Wasserstein error to well under one percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.69,0:05:01.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}often around a few hundredths,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.72,0:05:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while the best previous solver sits between about one and eighteen percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.80,0:05:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the MSCI single-cell task,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.77,0:05:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB reaches energy distance comparable to strong GPU baselines,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.30,0:05:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but it trains in roughly one to two and a half minutes on just four CPU cores,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.58,0:05:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whereas competing continuous solvers need tens of minutes to over an hour on a V100 GPU.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.54,0:05:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And on FFHQ faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.76,0:05:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it performs realistic male-to-female and child-to-adult translation in a five-hundred-twelve-dimensional latent space,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.75,0:05:36.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}converging in under a minute on CPU.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.49,0:05:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To understand the role of the noise parameter epsilon,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.72,0:05:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors map a two-dimensional Gaussian to a Swiss roll while sweeping epsilon across three values.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.94,0:05:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When epsilon is small,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.17,0:05:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the learned process is nearly deterministic and its trajectories are almost straight lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.39,0:05:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As epsilon grows,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.62,0:06:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the trajectories become more volatile and the conditional distributions at the endpoint spread out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.85,0:06:05.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This matches the theory: epsilon controls the stochasticity of the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.07,0:06:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The benchmark results also reveal that LightSB gains the most when the target distributions
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.30,0:06:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}align with its Gaussian-mixture inductive bias,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.52,0:06:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while remaining accurate across the tested dimensions and noise levels.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.05,0:06:21.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.21,0:06:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB converges in under one minute on four CPU cores for the five-hundred-twelve-dimensional
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.41,0:06:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}image translation task,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.91,0:06:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with no GPU at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.15,0:06:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the hardest single-cell setting, one thousand dimensions,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.07,0:06:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it reaches an energy distance of one point two seven in one hundred forty-six seconds on CPU,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.15,0:06:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}matching a minimax GPU solver that needs seventy-one minutes on a V100.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.79,0:06:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the entropic transport benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.14,0:06:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}its conditional error drops to as little as three hundredths of a percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.97,0:06:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}against best-baseline errors ranging from about one to eighteen percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.68,0:07:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And all of this comes with a theoretical guarantee: LightSB is a universal approximator of Schrödinger Bridges,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.93,0:07:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with generalization error that vanishes at the standard parametric rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.93,0:07:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message is that a Schrödinger Bridge solver does not have to be heavy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.31,0:07:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By parameterizing the transport potential as a Gaussian mixture and optimizing a single,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.08,0:07:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}straightforward objective,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.78,0:07:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LightSB solves entropic optimal transport and Schrödinger Bridges in minutes on a CPU,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.42,0:07:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}without adversarial training or process simulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.76,0:07:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It matches or outperforms much heavier GPU-based solvers,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.50,0:07:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}comes with a universal-approximation guarantee, and is easy to use.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.89,0:07:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In short, LightSB is positioned to be the simple,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.11,0:07:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reliable baseline that the Schrödinger Bridge field has been missing.
